-- title:
--   Artin approximation library, file 03: solutions in étale neighbourhoods, Tougeron's lemma with strong congruence, the induction step
-- statement:
--   Part 3 of 4 of a library proving Artin's approximation theorem at a rational point (M. Artin 1969, Theorem 1.10, étale-neighbourhood form): for a perfect field $K$, a finite-type $K$-algebra $A$ and a $K$-point $\chi : A \to K$, a solution in the $(\ker\chi)$-adic completion $\hat{A}$ of a finite polynomial system over $A$ gives a solution with the same residues in an étale neighbourhood of $\chi$. Everything is stated in Mathlib terms (`MvPolynomial`, `MvPowerSeries`, `AdicCompletion`, `Algebra.Etale`, `Algebra.TensorProduct`). Imports `Def_RPLib_FX_ArtinApprox_02`. Contents, in dependency order:
--
--   * the power-series solution of the coefficient system;
--   * solutions in étale neighbourhoods of the origin of $K[x_1, \dots, x_n]$, and their transport along automorphisms of the base;
--   * Tougeron's lemma with the strong congruence;
--   * linear algebra for the Jacobian datum, the chain rule, rows from a minor, and the $y$-minor at a power-series point;
--   * the Tougeron stage and the finishing step of the induction on the number of variables, and the statement `AA n` (Artin approximation for $K[x_1, \dots, x_n]$ at the origin) with the glue for the induction step.
-- source:
--   M. Artin, Algebraic approximation of structures over complete local rings, Publ. Math. IHÉS 36 (1969), 23–58; J.-C. Tougeron, Idéaux de fonctions différentiables, Springer (1972); H. Matsumura, Commutative Ring Theory, Cambridge University Press (1986), Chapters 8 and 10

